## 2. Industry Best Practices

### NBAstuffer: Critical Betting Statistics

**Source**: [NBA Stats for Bettors](https://www.nbastuffer.com/nba-stats-for-bettors/)

**Essential Metrics**:

#### Advanced Stats
- **PER (Player Efficiency Rating)** - Overall player value
- **TS% (True Shooting Percentage)** - Accounts for FTs and 3PM value
- **BPM (Box Plus/Minus)** - Team impact estimation

#### Team Metrics
- **Offensive Rating** - Points per 100 possessions
- **Defensive Rating** - Points allowed per 100 possessions
- **Pace** - Possessions per 48 minutes

#### Situational Factors
1. **Home/Away Splits** - Home teams win ~60% of games
2. **Rest Days** - Critical for back-to-backs (B2B)
   - 3rd or 4th game in 5 nights = fatigue indicator
   - Guards most affected (cover 5+ miles per game)
3. **Injury Reports** - Star player absence changes team dynamics
4. **Matchup History** - Some teams have stylistic advantages

**Application to S.A.V.A.G.E.**:
- Integrate TS% instead of raw FG% for efficiency
- Use Offensive/Defensive Rating as pace modifiers
- Apply B2B fatigue tax (especially for guards)
- Build matchup-specific defensive scheme adjustments

